WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.960
"Castle" followed a tried-and-true TV formula.

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:08.360
Nathan Fillion starred as crime novelist Richard
Castle and Stana Katic played homicide detective

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.380
Kate Beckett.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:13.889
The two mismatched characters improbably paired
up to solve crimes in New York City.

00:00:13.889 --> 00:00:18.390
Though Kate initially resented Castle being
around, the romantic tension between the two

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.850
couldn't be ignored, and they struck up a
romantic relationship.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:25.080
Behind the scenes, sparks also flew, but in
a bad way.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:30.490
In 2015, tensions supposedly came to a head,
and Katic suddenly exited the show after eight

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.320
seasons as one of the leads.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.410
There were rumors that Fillion demanded she
be written off the show, though his only public

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:41.280
statement about the situation was a 2016 Twitter
post in which he thanked Katic and wished

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:41.912
her well.

00:00:41.912 --> 00:00:47.631
In a 2018 interview with Entertainment Weekly,
Katic finally opened up about her firing, saying,

00:00:47.631 --> 00:00:51.210
"I'm actually still not clear on the thought
process behind the way that it went down.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.590
It hurt, and it was a harsh ending."

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:58.890
ABC canceled "Castle" in 2016, before a Katic-less
ninth season could be made.

